subject: security(auth): eliminate hardcoded default password acceptance (GAP-P1-14)

The login route previously accepted '123456' as a fallback when no password
hash was stored and no INITIAL_PASSWORD env was set. The mustChangePassword
gate only triggered for non-local requests, but tunnel/Tailscale clients
terminate on loopback — isLocalRequest() returned true for them, letting
remote users authenticate with the well-known default.

Fix: when no hash AND no INITIAL_PASSWORD exist, login ALWAYS rejects with
setupRequired=true regardless of request origin. A new /api/auth/setup
endpoint (local-only POST) lets the operator create the first password
from the machine itself. The login page detects setup state via GET and
shows a dedicated setup form.

- Login route: setup gate after SSO check, no recordFail on state condition
- Setup endpoint: isLocalRequest guard, bcrypt hash, 6-char minimum
- dashboardGuard: /api/auth/setup added to PUBLIC_API_PATHS
- Login page: setupRequired probe, setup form with confirm field
- 14 unit tests covering all branches (login gate + setup endpoint)

